%I A399029 #12 Aug 20 2026 16:56:56
%S A399029 1,1,1,2,7,41,399,6556,188337,9677605,902023153,154010835926,
%T A399029 48532168058199,28399574073907297
%N A399029 Number of nonisomorphic asymmetric tournaments on n vertices.
%C A399029 The values were obtained using the subgroup lattice of S_n and Möbius inversion.
%D A399029 J. W. Moon, Tournaments with a Given Automorphism Group, Canadian Journal of Mathematics, 16 (1964), 485-489.
%D A399029 J. W. Moon, Topics on Tournaments, Holt, Rinehart and Winston, New York, 1968.
%H A399029 Vladeta Jovovic, <a href="/A399029/a399029.pdf">Computational Enumeration of Asymmetric Tournaments</a>
%F A399029 a(n) = (1/n!) * Sum_{K <= S_n, |K| odd} mu(E,K) * 2^r(K), where mu is the Möbius function of the subgroup lattice of S_n and r(K) is the number of K-orbits on the 2-element subsets of {1,...,n}.
%e A399029 There are 7 nonisomorphic asymmetric tournaments on 5 vertices and 41 nonisomorphic asymmetric tournaments on 6 vertices.
%Y A399029 Cf. A000568 (number of nonisomorphic tournaments on n vertices).
%K A399029 nonn,hard,more
%O A399029 1,4
%A A399029 _Vladeta Jovovic_, Aug 17 2026
